    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d696">

                <pb facs="0676" n="666" sameAs="frus:frus1941v05/pg666"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/7229: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-06-19T13:00:00+07:00">June 19, 1941—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:08 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>246. To the Secretary of State from A. M. Fox.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“Conference with Generalissimo on the 14th highly satisfactory. Expressed
                        satisfaction at further evidence of American aid, complete agreement with
                        need for correction of China’s economic problems, and with Stabilization
                        Board’s coordinating its activities with alleviation of pending financial
                        and economic conditions.</p>
                    <p>Chinese members, Fox and Taylor<anchor n="6" xml:id="d696-f1"/> have held
                        number of informal and profitable discussions. Conference with leading
                        bankers and economists also going forward with Dr. Kung’s approval. Chinese
                        members together with Frese<anchor n="7" xml:id="d696-f2"/> are making short
                        fact-finding tour of leading Chinese cities while Fox and Taylor and
                        American trained Chinese economist are visiting Shanghai. Formal
                        organization Board deferred until it reassembles.[”]</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d696-f1" n="6" xml:id="d696-f1-content">
                <p>William H. Taylor, alternate American member of the China Stabilization Fund
                    Board and assistant to Dr. Fox.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d696-f2" n="7" xml:id="d696-f2-content">
                <p>Walter F. Frese, American assistant to Dr. Fox and Mr. Taylor.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
